p.note('Final black-ink sheet, pencil foliation 13; no date or author’s circled number. The upper part relates involutive bitorseurs, involutions of Ens(π), and extensions by Z/2, with the nonidentity fibre singled out. Below two long separator arrows it starts a definition of an I-weighted polygonal map, abandons a presentation, writes the free product of copies of Z/2, and draws its parity sequence and a numbered polygon map.')
p.note('The μ arrow is visibly leftward, contrary to H. The live and cancelled group signs below are capital Π. The cancelled relation has λi and a squared last generator, so the tempting ordinary single-product relation in H is not copied. The abbreviation is comb., and carte/gonale/pondérée are singular. The lower arrow label has the outline of 2 and is preserved even though an isomorphism mark would be natural; the denominator remains only a dash. The small isolated I-indexed curve is newly marked C|S.')
p.note('The drawing has thirteen written vertex labels: three 0s, one 1, three 2s and six 3s. Each of the two top quadrilaterals has three sloping hatches crossed by one opposite diagonal; an additional long pencil construction line passes through the left face. Fine pencil overlaps are approximated in TikZ, with the separate ink gaps and arrowheads retained. The brown incomplete ring at the far upper left follows a paper blemish and is not treated as an authorial symbol.')
p.check('141-014-even-free-product-kernel','targeted proof check','For the free product of n involutions a0,…,a(n−1), send every generator to the nontrivial element of Z/2. Using coset representatives 1,a0, the kernel has generators ai a0 for i>0 and their inverses a0 ai; the relators ai² supply only inverse-pair cancellations. Hence the kernel is free of rank n−1. This checks the usual interpretation of the displayed parity sequence, but does not supply any missing denominator or change the written 2-shaped label.')
p.habit('The last b of comb. has a small lower bowl and a rising stem, while the preceding m is nearly horizontal. Capital Π here has a very broad bar and two complete uprights, repeatedly misread as π by H. The label 2 has one diagonal body and a long foot; compare the two separate curves of wr on 013. Deep cancellations leave partial words and indices and are not replaced by complete expected formulas.')
p.notation('Π_I; Π_I+; (Z/2)^*I','Broad capital Π in both presentations and both sequence positions; plus raised; free-product star followed by I raised.')
p.notation('2-shaped vertical label; isolated C/S','Single hooked diagonal with foot is read 2; separate I-indexed open curve remains cal C|fraktur S.')
